    {
      "id": "56rmjwk",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Foundation of the Mughal Empire"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Mughal Empire was founded by Babur, who ruled from 1526 to 1530.",
        "Key rulers shaping the empire include Babur, Humayun, Akbar the Great, Jahangir, Shah Jahan, and Aurangzeb.",
        "Mughal Administration, along with Art and Architecture, formed the structural and cultural backbone of the empire.",
        "The gradual decline of the Mughal Empire marks a crucial transition period in Indian history frequently assessed in competitive exams."
      ],
      "id": "qok7xcn"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uk02rnw",
      "content": "• Babur, a descendant of Timur and Genghis Khan, founded the Mughal Empire."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ll6nwtp",
      "content": "• He defeated Ibrahim Lodi in the First Battle of Panipat in 1526."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "o7qyg0v",
      "content": "• The victory marked the beginning of Mughal rule in India."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xpxa75g",
      "content": "• Babur also fought important battles like the Battle of Khanwa (1527) against Rana Sanga."
    },
    {
